<header><p class="st-kicker">princely state · Indian princely states</p><h1 class="st-title">Siba State</h1><p class="st-meta">1450 CE – 1830 CE (approx.) · capital Siba</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A tiny Rajput hill state in the Kangra region, an offshoot of Guler, absorbed into the Sikh Empire in the early 19th century.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Siba was founded by a branch of the ruling family of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/guler-state">Guler State</a>, itself descended from the Katoch dynasty of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kangra-state">Kangra</a>; tradition places the split in the 15th century.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Siba was a small state of a few villages and forts in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beas">Beas</a> valley, with little recorded history of its own.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/sikh-empire">Sikh Empire</a> took control of Siba around 1830, and after 1846 the British confirmed the family in a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jagir">jagir</a>. The area is now in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kangra-state">Kangra</a> district, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/himachal-pradesh">Himachal Pradesh</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/siba-state.jpg" alt="Siba State" width="320" height="217"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sketch_map_of_Siba_State,_1882.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1450 CE – 1830 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>princely state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Siba</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hinduism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Kangri</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/india">India</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Siba</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1640&amp;focus=siba-state" aria-label="Siba State on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6640 1016 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Siba State lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6960 1272L6918 1285"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6918 1285h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6960 1272h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6960 1272h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1640&amp;focus=siba-state">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

